<div class="mp">

<h2>What transitions.dev says, and what is inference</h2>
<p>The site is a library of 32 copy-and-paste CSS transitions with a motion-token scale behind them, packaged as an agent skill. Its guidance that is stated in its own words: closes are faster and quieter than opens and are never delayed; overshoot belongs to entrances only; match a value on what the motion does, never on the nearest number; keep stagger totals under about 300&thinsp;ms; every snippet ships a reduced-motion guard that collapses to an instant state change with no movement, blur or scale; nothing depends on motion alone; motion sticks to compositor-friendly properties (transform, opacity, filter). Its scale is shorter than the app's: 80 to 500&thinsp;ms, blur 2 to 8&thinsp;px, pre-scales 0.96 to 0.99, bouncy easings for badges.</p>
<figure aria-label="Two duration scales side by side: transitions.dev's seven tokens from 80 to 500 milliseconds, and Firstmate 3000's three from 160 to 700 milliseconds">
<svg viewBox="0 0 510 214" width="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="var(--font-ui)" font-size="12.5">
