<p>Closes and dismissals are instant everywhere: a card leaving, a body collapsing, a section leaving, a pane closing. State commits before motion every time: the aria state, the disabled bit and the DOM change on the click, and the motion follows them; nothing in the host waits for an animation to end (the picture viewer keeps its shipped exception, which reads the computed duration rather than assuming one). Entrances are keyframes on keyed nodes, so an interruption is a restart, never a queue; the existing transitions keep retargeting from wherever they are.</p>

<h2>Boundaries</h2>
