<ul>
<li><b>Performance.</b> New motion animates opacity and transform only; no <span class="t">filter</span>, no new <span class="t">backdrop-filter</span> (the card is the window's one blur layer and re-samples the character every frame), no height, width or grid-row tweens, no <span class="t">will-change</span>. Feed and Tasks rows animate only when born after their document, so a boot or a big push never animates a list. The <span class="t">feed:render</span> and <span class="t">now:render</span> measures stay inside their budgets.</li>
<li><b>Responsiveness.</b> A control's state is readable at the first animation frame after the click, as the card-action test already demands; a pending button still drops its transition; nothing is gated on <span class="t">transitionend</span>.</li>
<li><b>No continual motion.</b> No shimmer on "working", no pulse on a waiting row, no spinner: the character's ember and the crew orbit are the app's only perpetual motion and are out of this plan's scope.</li>
<li><b>No large layout shifts.</b> Card height, composer growth, a dock collapsing, rows reordering and the theme or wash changing stay hard cuts.</li>
</ul>

